  "restoration_note": "This kephalaion enumerates the Twelve Judges sent from the Father of Greatness — a single twelvefold articulation of Divine Truth's discriminating power. The text follows a tight ordinal-judge formula (ⲧⲧⲙⲁⲍ-N ⲛ̄ⲕⲣⲓⲧⲏⲥ ⲡⲉ + name + relative descriptor + judicial action), which strongly constrains nearly all small lacunae and word-internal restorations. Editor proposals were confirmed throughout for ordinal prefixes, kephalaion title, name completions (ϣⲁⲣⲡ ⲛ̄ⲣⲱⲙⲉ, ⲡⲣⲉⲥⲃⲉⲩⲧⲏⲥ, ⲡⲡⲣⲓⲉ, ⲡⲡⲁⲣⲑⲉⲛⲟⲥ, ⲡⲛⲟⲩⲥ ⲛⲟⲩⲁⲓⲛⲉ, ⲡⲣ̄ⲣⲟ ⲙ̄ⲡⲧⲁⲓⲟ), and the antithetical separation formulae (Light/Darkness, victorious/destroyed). The Counsel-as-Call-and-Hearing arc and the eschatological Pandareias gathering are clearly preserved. Larger lacunae in the seventh-judge section (lines 35-40), in the description of the share of the Enemy (60-63), and in the closing line (103) are left unrestored — too damaged to reconstruct without invention. The restoration logic is governed throughout by Lycopolitan ordinal morphology (ⲧⲧⲙⲁⲍ-), the recurrent ⲡⲉⲧⲁϩ- relative, and the lexicon's fixed forms for the named hypostases.",
